          {
            "typeName": "dsDescription",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<table><tr><td><p dir=\"ltr\">The tool ‘Impact Strategy Development: Questions Bank and Interview Guide’ consists of (1) a three step interview guide and (2) an Excel file with a questions bank to use and tailor for your interviews or other methods for engaging with your community throughout the process of developing a school-level impact strategy. The package also includes a set of auxiliary materials designed to inspire and enrich conversations during the interview.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><i>Who can primarily benefit from this tool?</i></b><br><i>Individuals and teams directly involved in the process of developing, implementing and evaluating impact strategies in their school.</i><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><i>In which context is this tool useful?</i></b><br><i>This tool is part of the Impact Strategy Development Toolkit. Use this tool to identify relevant questions and realise interviews and other community engagement approaches during the discovery and develop phases of strategy development. </i><i>It is based on first-hand experience</i><i> </i><i>with defining, exploring, and aligning</i><i> </i><i>societal impact strategies with the needs and identities of</i><i> </i><i>seve</i><i>ral schools at Erasmus University Rotterdam.</i><i> </i><i>While the tool follows the language and organisation within Erasmus University Rotterdam, it can also be used in other contexts and institutes.</i></p></td></tr></table><p></p>"
                }
              }
            ]
